    },
    {
      "text": "C. Andrieu, A. Doucet and R. Holenstein",
      "bbox": [
        78.57550048828125,
        39.52751922607422,
        237.29876708984375,
        47.82143783569336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "emphasize at this point that we do not believe that the resulting PIMH sampler that is presented",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        56.66524124145508,
        438.2300109863281,
        65.90057373046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "below is on its own a serious competitor to standard SMC approximations to pθ.x1:T |y1:T /.",
      "bbox": [
        42.70989990234375,
        67.78358459472656,
        438.2314147949219,
        79.39529418945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "However, as is the case with standard IMH-type updates, the PIMH update might be of inter-",
      "bbox": [
        42.711212158203125,
        80.57557678222656,
        438.2314453125,
        89.8109130859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "est when used in combination with other MCMC transitions. In Section 2.4.2, we describe",
      "bbox": [
        42.711212158203125,
        92.53071594238281,
        438.2314147949219,
        101.76605224609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the particle marginal Metropolis–Hastings (PMMH) algorithm which can be thought of as an",
      "bbox": [
        42.711212158203125,
        104.48585510253906,
        438.2303771972656,
        113.72119140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "exact approximation of a ‘marginal Metropolis–Hastings’ (MMH) update targeting directly",
      "bbox": [
        42.711212158203125,
        116.44099426269531,
        438.227294921875,
        125.67633056640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the marginal density p.θ|y1:T / of p.θ, x1:T |y1:T /. Finally, in Section 4.5 we present a particle",
      "bbox": [
        42.711212158203125,
        127.55928039550781,
        438.2320861816406,
        139.17123413085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximation to a Gibbs sampler targeting p.θ, x1:T |y1:T /, called hereafter the particle Gibbs",
      "bbox": [
        42.7109375,
        139.5147247314453,
        438.2301940917969,
        151.12643432617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
